_1","x":40,"y":-20,"w":230,"h":129,"text":"**One flow for every card.** Only if lets a click through while fewer than two cards are up. The card turns up, and the second one up counts a move and checks the pair.","colour":"sky","author":"Example","anchor":{"layerId":"lgm9bwt120fb1na","lx":0,"ly":-143}},{"id":"note_example_gn_tut_memory_2","x":1594,"y":173,"w":230,"h":94,"text":"**A miss waits a second**, then turns every card that is up back down. A match keeps both as matched instead.","colour":"sky","author":"Example","anchor":{"layerId":"lgm9bwt1dp9ae1d","lx":0,"ly":-108}}]},"clip":true,"notes":[{"id":"note_example_tut_memory_1","x":0,"y":636,"w":260,"h":144,"text":"**One Card, repeated.** *Cards* repeats its one button over the `cards` list, four to a row, so restyle the Card once and all twelve change. `item` is the card each copy shows.","author":"Example"},{"id":"note_example_tut_memory_2","x":276,"y":636,"w":260,"h":144,"text":"**The deal is a formula.** `cards` is worked out with `shuffle(..., seed)`. Showing the page adds 1 to `seed` and puts `cards` back to its start, which works the formula out again: a new order.","colour":"sky","author":"Example"}]},{"id":"abm9bwtm0wvgmc","name":"Well done","width":800,"height":600,"background":{"type":"solid","color":"token:tkm9bws3nm1yni"},"canvasX":920,"canvasY":0,"children":[{"id":"nm9bwt1mnxvqo6","type":"text","name":"Title","x":60,"y":120,"width":680,"height":54,"rotation":0,"scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"originX":0.5,"originY":0.5,"opacity":1,"visible":true,"fontFamily":"\"Open Sans\", system-ui, sans-serif","fontSize":40,"fontWeight":700,"fontStyle":"normal","lineHeight":1.3,"letterSpacing":0,"color":"token:tkm9bws6exnhmt","align":"center","verticalAlign":"top","text":"Well done!","autoSize":"height"},{"id":"nm9bwt1n3mtqre","type":"text","name":"Result","x":60,"y":200,"width":680,"height":30,"rotation":0,"scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"originX":0.5,"originY":0.5,"opacity":1,"visible":true,"fontFamily":"\"Open Sans\", system-ui,